The subscribe button flashes its momentary
beacon, the like button flickering as it points

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.259
its thumb up.

00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:13.049
The video ends, and YouTube autoplays another.

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:14.759
And the monkeys watch.

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:15.730
They don’t question.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.833
They sit.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:18.510
They consume.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.099
But now that’s changed.

00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:24.370
The truth we’ve unearthed will leave you
seeing things through new eyes.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.000
We are obsolete.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.689
So, ask yourself this.

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:33.150
How does it feel when a Theory becomes a fact?

00:00:35.891 --> 00:00:37.340
Hello Internet!

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.800
Welcome to Film Theory, the show that wants
you to think really, really hard about clicking

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.820
that subscribe button.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:44.820
Harder.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.439
Harder.

00:00:45.439 --> 00:00:45.939
You know what?

00:00:45.939 --> 00:00:46.544
I think it worked.

00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:50.600
Today, we're returning to the terrifying world
of the Mandela Catalogue, an analog horror

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.239
series created by Alex Kister right here on
YouTube.com.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.710
In case you’re just catching up, the story
takes place in Mandela County, a fictional

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:02.530
part of Wisconsin, where an unknown man called
the intruder keeps appearing on TV, causing

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.420
children to suddenly vanish.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.690
Now, that alone would be terrifying.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:11.140
But in addition to weird televised kidnappers,
the world is also dealing with a race of creepy

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:16.180
doppelgangers called alternates, twisted beings
that drive people insane and cause a lot of

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.360
death before going on to steal their identities.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.890
In short, the world Alex is building here
brings together tons of big ideas from religion,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.670
horror and old school science fiction, and
then mixes it with a visual style

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.860
that's one part Blair Witch, one part PlayStation
1 era cut scene and a little VeggieTale nightmare

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.260
fuel thrown in on the side for flavor.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.170
Since our last theory, a lot has happened
in this universe, there have been two brand

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:42.729
new volumes uploaded on to Alex's channel,
an entire ARG website that's come and gone,

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:47.620
even a couple of videos covering the element
most crucial to solving this thing: The plushies!

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.690
That's right friendos, mark the occasion for
the first time ever in 12 years of theorizing,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:57.350
we got ourselves some plushie lore because
this is going to be the thing that cracks

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.640
the whole series wide open.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:01.075
But in all seriousness, it is actually going
to play an important role in the theory that

00:02:01.075 --> 00:02:02.075
we have coming out today.

00:02:02.075 --> 00:02:05.600
So today in a series where there's a lot of
characters and a lot of stuff going on.I want

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.619
to focus on the big picture stuff.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:09.080
Who is the intruder?

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.250
What are the alternates?

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:14.069
Why is there an early 2000s amateur ghost
hunting crew mixed up with all of this?

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:17.518
And how is it possibly relevant to all the
biblical inter-dimensional stuff that keeps

00:02:17.518 --> 00:02:18.518
popping up?

00:02:18.518 --> 00:02:22.560
Well, my friends, I suspect that all of it
is a battle over a man who will become the

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.400
future of the human race.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.174
We've got a lot to cover today, Loyal Theorists.

00:02:26.174 --> 00:02:28.474
So pop in your contraband VHS tape.

00:02:28.474 --> 00:02:29.594
It's time to watch.

00:02:30.937 --> 00:02:34.640
So one of the biggest and most obvious unanswered
questions about the series is what's going

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.114
on with all its religious imagery?

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:37.894
Since its very first upload, Overthrown,

00:02:37.894 --> 00:02:42.360
The Mandela Catalogue’s incorporated animated
biblical stories into its narrative.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.530
But we're not talking about your typical Sunday
school lessons here, friends.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.590
These are a bit off.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.690
Across the uploads we watch a being known
as Gabriel infiltrate classic biblical stories

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:52.620
from Adam and Eve to Noah and the Ark.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.801
Each time he comes bearing an important and
seemingly dangerous message.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.910
But Gabriel here isn't just sending messages
down from on high.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.340
He's determined to get his hands dirty.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.420
In the most recent upload, volume 4,

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.549
We see that Gabriel is a literal being that
can manifest in reality, communicate with

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:18.916
normal humans, and then kill the people he
encounters.

00:03:28.313 --> 00:03:32.440
Now, in earlier theories, I suspected that
Gabriel might be some sort of alien taking

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.700
the shape of an angel.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.939
That might seem strange, but in the first
ever upload of the series, we actually get

00:03:36.939 --> 00:03:40.940
this brief glimpse of a strange alien face
that eventually gets censored.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.595
And while I suspect that still may be true,
what is undeniable now at this point in the

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:48.800
series is that Gabriel is also this story's
stand-in for the devil.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.080
He is this world's version of Satan.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.470
At the beginning of volume 4, we see a retelling
of the biblical story of Genesis, and we speed

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.750
run through all the highlights: the formation
of the world in seven days, the division of

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.950
land and sea, the creation of man in the form
of Adam and Eve, and their eventual downfall

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:07.019
when they're convinced to eat an apple from
the Tree of Knowledge, which prompts God to

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:08.110
yeet them out of paradise.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.050
Now, in most retellings of the story, a snake
is the one who offers the apple a snake that

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.190
is symbolic of Satan himself, tempting man
and causing their downfall.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.729
But here in the Mandela Catalogue’s version
of events, Gabriel is the one that's responsible

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:23.760
for this, thereby equating him with Satan.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.360
This suddenly makes a lot of other details
about the series click into place.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:32.190
For example, in the upload Exhibition, Gabriel
tells Noah to bring an unexpected passenger

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.170
on the ark, one that will carry a secret message.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.370
The screen then goes dark and the audio goes
silent, but the closed captions continue with

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:40.460
a hidden message.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.100
They reference 2 Corinthians 11:14 quote,
“And no wonder!

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.350
for Satan disguises himself as an angel of
light.”

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.500
That is literally what's happening here.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.560
Gabriel is disguising himself as a very traditional
looking, Renaissance era statuesque angel.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.130
Satan is disguised.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:00.020
Additionally, we see the number 333 show up
multiple times throughout the series as both

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:05.646
the title of the third upload volume 333 as
well as the highway exit that leads to Mandela County.

00:05:05.646 --> 00:05:09.980
Again, Gabriel being Satan disguised as an
angel of light ties all of that together.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:15.140
333 is often considered to be the number of
angels and it references how 3 is a holy number

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:19.430
to a lot of Christians because it represents
the Trinity; God split between three entities:

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.780
the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:27.690
But 333 is also half of 666, the number of
the beast, often associated with Satan.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.900
So the number works symbolically in multiple
ways.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:34.220
Mandela is a town controlled by this evil
angel 333, the number of angels, but it's

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.800
also a marker for an onramp to Satan's domain.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.639
So what then is Gabriel's plan?

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.370
What is his evil message?

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.350
Well, basically, Gabriel's a symbol that weaponizes
religion.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.540
He's made it so that religion that the church
itself is a cult.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.460
And we know this based on the most recent
upload in volume 4, there's an ongoing threat

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:55.540
of conversation between Dave Lee, owner of
a failing video store, and his friend O'Brien,

00:05:55.540 --> 00:06:00.530
a guy who plays in a band and offers to get
Dave a job at the local church if his video

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.870
store gig falls through.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.913
Dave begins the upload by rejecting his offer.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.849
Flash forward two years later, though, and
the store actually has to close, prompting

00:06:13.849 --> 00:06:15.349
Dave to have a change of heart.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.789
Dave covers up his TVs, symbolizing him turning
his back on technology and his old way of

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:30.009
doing things before he heads off to the church
to meet with his friend.

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:34.440
But there he's locked out when he calls O'Brien
to let him in, Gabriel appears.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.562
And Gabriel uses the same words that O'Brien
just said to him over the phone.

00:06:38.562 --> 00:06:39.857
Stay still.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.780
O'Brien was an agent of Gabriel.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.750
Dave is killed because he ultimately turned
to religion.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.720
He's now yet another victim of Gabriel's.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.389
As for O'Brien, he was yet another example
of this world's alternates, the creepy, elongated

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:57.588
beings with their ability to mimic humans.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.830
And we now know that alternates are confirmed
to be Gabriel's minions.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:09.889
Recently, the creator Alex Kister launched
a merch campaign, releasing an official makeshift

00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:11.289
figurine of Gabriel.

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:15.040
Where the character is described as, quote,
“The harbinger of evil” and “the first

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.040
alternate”.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.960
But while he may have been the first, his
alternate army has been spreading that message

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.850
to Noah as they prepare to board the ark.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.479
The entity that's hopping on board is likely
an early alternate.

00:07:25.479 --> 00:07:30.580
In the merch drop Gabriel is also described
as a hivemind leader, so all the other alternates

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:31.819
are parts of him.

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:35.320
Come to think of it, maybe Gabriel really
is an alien after all, because all of this

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:38.740
sounds a lot like John Carpenter's classic
horror flick The Thing.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.460
In that film, an alien is uncovered in Antarctica
that's able to shapeshift and steal the identities

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.870
of the people that it touches.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.360
Adding them to its hivemind.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:50.350
Sounds a lot like what Gabriel is doing throughout
Mandella, and it's here where we find our

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.100
second big question about the series.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:55.919
If alternates are such a big threat, why Is
the government not doing anything about them?

00:07:55.919 --> 00:08:00.449
The world is oddly complacent about these
creatures that are stealing identities and

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:01.910
in the process killing thousands.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.050
So, again, what is going on?

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:07.629
Well, based on the evidence, it seems likely
that the government has been infiltrated by

00:08:07.629 --> 00:08:09.129
Gabriel and his alternates.

00:08:09.129 --> 00:08:10.129
Let me explain.

00:08:10.129 --> 00:08:13.440
The earliest government record of alternates
that we see in the series appears in the form

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:18.210
of a 1980s public service announcement from
the U.S. Department of Temporal Phenomena.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:22.639
Here, they warn people to keep every entrance
to their home secured and to keep a firearm

00:08:22.639 --> 00:08:24.180
on them at all times for self-defense.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.198
In fact, all civilians are encouraged to fight
back against the alternates.

00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:41.250
By the 1990s, though, the tactics definitely
seemed to have changed.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:46.330
Police dispatchers in Mandela County are actively
told not to help callers reporting alternate

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:47.330
attacks.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:50.680
In fact, they're told to actively lie to tell
the caller that everything's going to be okay.

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:54.710
Then wait until the caller stops responding,
presumably after they die.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:58.399
It's certainly a far cry from the earlier
advice of Kill It with Fire.

00:08:58.399 --> 00:09:01.960
Another decade later, during the portion of
the story that takes place in the late 2000s,

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:07.399
the government now seems to be actively targeting
people looking into or interfering with alternates.

00:09:07.399 --> 00:09:12.610
We see in volume 2 that two characters named
Adam and Jonah are wanted by the FBI because

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:17.220
they're possibly associated with the Bythorne
Paranormal Society, a group of ghost hunters

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.330
who sometimes search for alternates.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.760
Why would the FBI, of all people, be interested
in a bunch of young kids looking into the

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.829
existence of ghosts unless they were trying
to silence anyone who might learn the truth

00:09:27.829 --> 00:09:29.340
about the alternate threat?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:33.180
It's also, at this point in the timeline,
after a decade plus of complete inaction when

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.805
people have just totally given up on government
officials helping with pretty much anything

00:09:36.805 --> 00:09:37.828
in this world.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:48.630
These massive changes in messaging and how
to deal with alternates would make sense if

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:53.060
the government were somehow in on Gabriel's
plan, either infected by his message or with

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:56.570
key people in positions of power replaced
by alternates.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.450
So Gabriel is literally the devil, and he's
using his army of alternates to infiltrate

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.450
the police and government.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:05.089
That being said, one thing that's still unclear
to me in the series is just how widespread

00:10:05.089 --> 00:10:09.209
the alternate threat is for there to be an
entire government agency like the U.S. Department

00:10:09.209 --> 00:10:13.190
of Temporal Phenomena, issuing warnings about
how to prevent the alternate threat.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:16.020
That would seem to suggest that these things
are nationwide.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.869
But so far, everything we've seen from the
series has been local to Mandela and its surrounding counties.

00:10:20.869 --> 00:10:24.810
It seems so localized, in fact, that one character
we meet even questions whether alternates

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:25.717
are real.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:34.610
I suspect what we're witnessing here are the
beginnings of the alternates' global takeover,

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:39.490
their start in Mandela, the epicenter of activity
and subsequent spread to other nearby counties,

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:44.620
a spread that's being slowed or even outright
halted by the other key figure in the series

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:48.690
and the other major mystery that's going on
here, the intruder, the mysterious man in

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.269
the TV responsible for stealing kids out of
their homes and doing. . .

00:10:52.269 --> 00:10:55.190
Well, we were never quite sure about what
he was doing.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.700
At least we weren't until now.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:01.209
You see, with the most recent upload, I think
we now know the answer to this one too.

00:11:01.209 --> 00:11:05.649
One of the strangest sections from volume
333 is an extended segment taken from a mysterious

00:11:05.649 --> 00:11:09.490
short film called Might of the Subconscious,
a film made by a production company that's

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.970
impossible to track down.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:14.380
We know that fact, thanks to an ARG website
that launched earlier this year.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:18.589
In Might of the Subconscious, we meet Stanley,
a face made out of simple white lines who

00:11:18.589 --> 00:11:20.268
claims to want new friends.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:27.820
Given Stanley's tone, this is clearly meant
to be shown to children.

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:32.358
As he goes on, though, things become a bit
strange as Stanley claims to be able to…

00:11:35.209 --> 00:11:38.709
He asks the viewer to imagine every detail
of their ideal friend.

00:11:38.709 --> 00:11:40.574
Then, in a segment that glitches out, Stanley
says:

00:11:45.779 --> 00:11:50.279
As the subtitles continue and complete the
sentence to say: “to manifest them instead.”

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:53.760
At the end of the segment, Stanley says that
he thinks it worked and that the new friend

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.160
is somewhere in the house.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:12:00.000
It's at that point we hard cut to a police
call of someone panicked of an intruder in their home.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.670
An alternate has been manifested, the caller
disappears, and Ruth Weaver, one of the police

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.070
investigators, ultimately winds up killed.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.120
But who is Stanley?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.510
Who would have the power to summon twisted
monsters like this?

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.510
It's the intruder.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.848
In volume 4 the intruder basically confirms
that he was Stanley all along.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.990
This also plays into the intruders use of
televisions.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:40.260
He's using them to show his face to as many
people as possible, cementing his creepy features

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.260
in their minds.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:45.260
And then the old videotape is basically a
tutorial for children to literally think him

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:49.529
and his alternates into reality, which now
sets the stage for the big picture story that's

00:12:49.529 --> 00:12:54.709
going on in the Mandela Catalogue a story
of two competing false gods, a false god within

00:12:54.709 --> 00:12:59.760
religion in the form of Gabriel, and another
false god within the television, the intruder,

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.970
an alternate who's gone rogue from Gabriel's
army.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.140
And the two of them are constantly trading
blows.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:08.700
While Gabriel replaces people with alternate,
twisted versions of themselves.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:13.560
The intruder counters by manifesting into
our reality and snatching children away before

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.490
they can be corrupted or worse.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:19.750
See, though, this doesn't apply in every denomination,
several sects of Christianity view dying in

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.089
the way that alternates end lives a sin.

00:13:22.089 --> 00:13:25.220
A sin that dooms the soul to H-E double hockey
sticks.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:29.829
And if Gabriel is Satan, well, wouldn't that
mean that he gets more powerful with every

00:13:29.829 --> 00:13:31.400
life ended in this way?

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:35.360
That would also explain why some of the instructions
given by the Department of Temporal Phenomena

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.360
in their T.H.I.N.K.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:40.491
initiative tell civilians to…
because there's not enough room for the two of us.

00:13:40.491 --> 00:13:45.790
It's the government under Gabriel's control,
giving directions that make Gabriel more powerful.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:50.389
Gabriel also counters the intruder by having
the USDTP order all TV screens and mirrors

00:13:50.389 --> 00:13:54.010
be destroyed, rendering the screen hopping
intruder useless.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.899
And this campaign also winds up wildly successful.

00:13:56.899 --> 00:14:01.120
Seeing old TVs turned on is a big deal in
this world enough so that one character keeps

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:05.889
an old CRT television hidden under a blanket
in his closet like contraband, claiming it's

00:14:05.889 --> 00:14:08.839
the last one in the entire state of Wisconsin.

00:14:08.839 --> 00:14:09.574
But why?

00:14:09.574 --> 00:14:12.579
Sure, maybe these forces are just duking it out
for some sort of control.

00:14:12.579 --> 00:14:14.440
But aren't they both alternate?

